<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Binnya U</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1323">1323</a>–<a href="/years/1384">1384</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Binnya U was king of the Mon kingdom of Martaban–Hanthawaddy in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1348 to 1384. His long reign was troubled by rebellions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> and attacks from neighbouring states, and in 1369 he moved the capital from Martaban to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a>. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razadarit">Razadarit</a>, who restored the kingdom's strength and unity.</p></div>
